CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicit argument and a pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member trailing return type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ deduced pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
guess_function_template_args expanded the single placeholder of a directly
deduced pack only while draining deferred method bodies; outside every
function body it now expands it too.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
